{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Suppose the position function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b4c546781141a58a3baeb807f41c1acaec8056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(t) = -16t^{2} - 10t + 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"21\" /> gives the height in feet of a falling rock at time <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> seconds. What is the velocity of the rock at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80d4822fd227ceb0ef72b1bd9326703a98f8593c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=2$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> seconds?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffea5c77fba06b50a9c5fd6408cf7a98d41a3c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -16 \\text{ feet per second}  \\quad \\textbf{(B)}\\ -22 \\text{ feet per second}  \\quad \\textbf{(C)}\\ -32 \\text{ feet per second}  \\quad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 16 \\text{ feet per second}  \\quad \\textbf{(E)}\\ -42\\text{ feet per second}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"992\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Note: This problem was omitted because the options A-E were incorrect.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The velocity is the derivative of position, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f700bfea6aaf9cf1e4122229d0141546e277792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v(t) = s&#39;(t) = -32t - 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"194\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/921916026ad804370f042467560a8689b9225953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v(2) = -32(2) - 10 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(F)}\\ -74 \\text{ feet per second}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"378\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus